LDT Test Case for "Add multiple crop and multiple irrigation type support in LDT"-- Github issue #106
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This test-case produces the LIS input file required to run Noah3.6 with the new
irrigation Scheme over the global domain.
Used in the GLIrr simulation in Rodell et al. 2026 JAMES paper.


This directory contains:

* this README file.
* it requres LDT to be compiled in multiple processor mode and executed with 4 or more processors for the global domain. See the job script run_ldt.job.
* the ldt.config file used for this test case.
* input directory with all input files that are needed to run this test case.
* lis_input_testcase.d01.nc created LIS input file by this test case.
* ldtlog_testcase.000[0-3] log file generated by the test case.
* input.ctl: GrADS description file for viewing lis_input_testcase.d01.nc for landcover (z=46) dimensions. 
* input_croptypes.ctl: GrADS description file for viewing lis_input_testcase.d01.nc for croptype (z=26) dimensions. 
* input_irrtypes.ctl: GrADS description file for viewing lis_input_testcase.d01.nc for irrigtype (z=3) dimensions. 

Note: The landcover scheme of MODIS-IGBP (NCEP-modified) has 20 classes including Cropland and Cropland/Natural Vegetation Mosaic.  The cropland classes are merged with MIRCA2000 dataset that includes 26 crop classes. Therefore, total landcover classes aand surface types are 46 where cropland classes (index 12 & 14) are set to zero and distributed among 26 crop classes (index 21-46).   
The crop fracions are saved as croptype when using MIRCA crop dataset, which represent a sum of irrigated and rainfed crop fractions saved as irrigcrop and rainfedcrop variables.  However, croptype fractions maybe scaled when there's descrepancy between GIA, GRIPC, MIRCA, and underlying land cover data.  The sum of irrigcrop maybe set to zero if GIA=0, then croptype is set to rainfedcrop to fulfill cropland land cover fraction.
